>> title: Steamed Artichoke with Lemon Aioli
>> servings: 2
>> time: 50 minutes
>> tags: exotic, watchme, vegetable, steaming, prep-heavy

-- watch: Stem is peeled to the pale tender center, with tough green exterior removed.
Trim @artichokes{2}, peel stems with a #vegetable peeler{}, and cut off the top inch with a #serrated knife{}.

-- watch: Leaf tips are clipped flat so thorny points are gone.
Snip sharp leaf tips with #kitchen shears{}.

Rub cut surfaces with @lemon{1/2} to slow browning.

Steam artichokes over @water{2%cups} in a #covered pot{} until a leaf pulls out easily, about ~{35%minutes}.

Mix @mayonnaise{1/3%cup}, @lemon juice{1%tbsp}, @garlic{1%clove}, and @kosher salt{1%pinch} in a #small bowl{}.

-- watch: Fuzzy choke is scraped away cleanly, leaving the smooth heart.
Halve cooked artichokes and scrape out the fuzzy choke with a #spoon{}.

Serve warm with lemon aioli.
